---
description: Work token-efficiently in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---
- Search before reading: use `rg` with tight patterns and globs; read only the matched ranges, never whole large files.
- Don't re-read files you already read this session unless they changed.
- Prefer `git diff --stat`/`gh pr diff` over reading full files when reviewing.
- Never open generated or vendor files (node_modules, bin/obj, dist, lockfiles, migrations you aren't changing).
- Run only the tests for what you touched (CI path filters mirror this); run the full suite once before opening the PR.
- Pipe noisy command output through `tail -n 50` or `--quiet` flags; don't paste full logs.
- Keep plans, commit messages and PR descriptions short and factual.
- Reuse existing components and patterns instead of writing new ones (also a project rule).
- For deeper guidance, use the `token-saver` skill.
